occupationalSummary:
&lt;p&gt;This occupation is found in construction and the built environment industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Construction site supervisors can work in a variety of settings such as residential, commercial, industrial, infrastructure construction, and civil engineering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The broad purpose of the occupation is to support with overseeing on-site construction operations. Construction site supervisors bridge the gap between senior managers and on-site teams. They ensure compliance with health and safety regulations, construction legislation and industry standards, according to the project plan and specifications. They coordinate workers, teams, and workflows to ensure a project progresses as intended.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In their daily work, an employee in this occupation interacts with a variety of stakeholders such as other construction workers, subcontractors, project managers, suppliers, site managers, and depending on the scale of the project, customers, architects, engineers, inspectors.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An employee in this occupation will be responsible for monitoring various aspect of a construction site – health and safety compliance, quality control, material and equipment project, and cost control. Construction site supervisors implement and enforce safety protocols based on a deep understanding of construction site hazards and regulations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They interpret architectural and engineering drawings and specifications to ensure accurate implementation of construction plans. They apply knowledge of construction materials, methods, and techniques to monitor and maintain quality standards throughout the project.&amp;nbsp; Construction site supervisors communicate technical aspects of the project to construction teams, subcontractors and other stakeholders to ensure activities adhere to regulatory requirements and specified standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
